    "description": {
      "value": "<p><em>Angle the Lens until truth appears.</em></p><p>Once per <strong>Strategic Turn</strong>, when your faction makes a <strong>Spark Identification</strong> roll (to determine the Lore or category of a Spark or key occult element), you can spend <strong>1 Intrigue OP</strong> to stabilize a bad read.</p><ul><li>If the 2d10x10 roll for that Identification check is <strong>9 or lower</strong>, you may treat the result as if it were a <strong>10</strong> instead.</li><li>This represents your ability to bend the investigation away from false positives and dead-end theories.</li></ul><p>This does not guarantee success; it just means your worst guess is at least passable.</p><div data-ft-per-use=\"1\" data-ft-per-use-key=\"wlTruthRefr\" style=\"margin-top:0.7rem;padding:0.55rem 0.75rem;border:1px solid #b08acc;border-radius:0.35rem;background:rgba(70,55,95,0.18);\">\n  <div style=\"font-size:0.78rem;letter-spacing:0.04em;text-transform:uppercase;color:#d4b8e8;margin-bottom:0.25rem\">⟁ Per-Use Ability — <strong>Truth Refraction</strong></div>\n  <div style=\"font-size:0.86rem;opacity:0.92;line-height:1.4\"><strong>Recovery:</strong> 1/Strategic Turn (1 Intrigue OP) &nbsp;·&nbsp; <strong>Action:</strong> Strategic &nbsp;·&nbsp; <strong>Use:</strong> Click this feature on your sheet to invoke.</div>\n  <div style=\"font-size:0.82rem;opacity:0.85;margin-top:0.3rem\">When your faction makes a Spark Identification roll, spend 1 Intrigue OP: if the 2d10x10 is 9 or lower, treat it as a 10 instead. Bends the investigation away from false positives — doesn't guarantee success.</div>\n</div>",
